<title>UK: BOE gives UK money market 336 mln stg further help.</title>
<headline>BOE gives UK money market 336 mln stg further help.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 336 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.  </p>
<p>The Bank allotted 117 million outright in bills maturing on or before May 7 and 219 million stg in repos to May 6 and 7.</p>
<p>It has now provided liquidity totalling 761 million stg in response to a forecast money market shortage of 1.9 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 5109</p>
